    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0477" n="465" xml:id="pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.00–N/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-17T16:00:00-04:00">June 17, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. The surrender of France has served to strengthen materially the hands of the
                    pro-Nazi elements here and that the Government is now faced with a situation
                    that might conceivably get out of hand. Without wishing to appear to exaggerate
                    the gravity of conditions, I feel strongly that our Government should take
                    prompt and energetic action to meet this danger.</p>
                <p>[Here follows a report of press comment.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
